  "details": "The ability to focus individually a layer (world layer, player layer) has its benefits for two reasons.\n\nDepth error - depth of field uses (obviously) the depth buffer. This leads to ghosting around edges of objects and can make photographs appear \"smudgy\" or emphasize aliasing issues.\n\nFocusing the camera takes effort - wouldn't it be cool if you could just take a selfie and have the focus work blurring the background every single time without needing to click a bunch of sliders to alleviate the issues mentioned above? ^^",
